    "created_at": "2025-11-26T10:20:21Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-11-26T10:20:21Z",
    "body": "If screen reader software has an a problem with a nested `aside` inside a `main` element then it is a screen reader bug and should be reported to the software vendor. \n\nThe informative content model for `<main>` is \n\n> Flow content, but with no main element descendants.\nsource: https://w3c.github.io/html-aria/#index-aria-main\n\nThe normative content model is\n\n> [Content model](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#concept-element-content-model):\n> [Flow content](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/dom.html#flow-content-2).\nsource: https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/grouping-content.html#the-main-element\n\nThe ARIA spec states:\n\n> A [landmark](https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/#landmark) that is designed to be complementary to the main content at a similar level in the DOM hierarchy, but remaining meaningful when separated from the main content.\nsource: https://www.w3.org/TR/wai-aria-1.2/#complementary\n\n_Similar_ does not mean it needs to be the same level in the DOM heirarchy.\n\nWhat problem(s) does using `aside/complimentary` cause people?\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "pin": null,
