    "body": "Perhaps MDN should be updated to explain that sometimes `aside` has a generic role, according to the [HTML a11y API mapping spec](https://w3c.github.io/html-aam/#el-aside):\n\n> [complementary](https://w3c.github.io/core-aam/#role-map-complementary) role if the [aside](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/sections.html#the-aside-element) element has an [accessible name](https://www.w3.org/TR/accname-1.2/#dfn-accessible-name). Otherwise, [generic](https://w3c.github.io/core-aam/#role-map-generic) role.",
