    "created_at": "2025-12-04T01:12:39Z",
    "updated_at": "2025-12-04T01:14:43Z",
    "body": "@LJWatson wrote:\n> Jaws and NVDA both have keyboard commands that let you move directly to the end of a containing element…\n[…snip…]\n> Off the top of my head I don't know if VoiceOver or TalkBack have similar capability, but if not, then it seems like something that might be useful. Either way, this feels like a screen reader problem to solve, not a spec change.\n\nIssue is now closed (I agree), but for completeness/posterity, VoiceOver has several ways to bypass content like this too… \n- navigate to next branch in the tree (VO+Shift+Right, rather than auto-step-into-container with VO+Right) bypassing any descendant nodes\n- move to end of current container (VO-End)\n- Find next different item (VO+Cmd+D) may also work here, depending on how the page is authored",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
